/* =====================================================================
   sentence-stage-core.js — the model for ACTIVITY #128 of the one-by-one
   rebuild: "Wiggles' Sentence Builder" → THE SENTENCE STAGE (L.1.1.j;
   all 11 locales).
   Design: docs/activities-rebuild/designs/128-sentence-builder.md
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   A sentence is a script and a toy theatre acts it out word by word: the
   start word opens the curtain, a number word lights that many spotlights,
   a describing word sizes or colours the light, the naming word brings the
   actor on, the doing word makes it act, and the end mark closes the
   curtain. The show freezes at the first word that is out of place.
   · levels 1–4 (build): the blocks of one sentence wait in the wings; the
     script is right only in the sentence's own order (level 1 shows the
     actor as a clue, level 2 does not, level 3 adds a separate full stop,
     level 4 asks and shouts with ? and ! — and es with ¿ ¡);
   · level 5 (write): a photo hangs by the stage; the child writes a
     sentence from a word bank (a determiner, two naming words, four
     describing words, three doing words, . and !) in the language's own
     order, with at most one describing word (two after a noun need a
     conjunction in fr/es/pt/it) — right when every word is true of the
     photo, and the one true doing word is what the photo shows.
   Every word is authored per locale (agreement, case, the es opening
   marks, the fr typographic space), never assembled. DATA is written by a
   build script. Pure and DOM-free; UMD (window.SentenceStageCore /
   require()).
   ===================================================================== */
